.TH AGENTMOVE 1 "2026-08-05" "agentmove-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agentmove \- move your AI agent between clients: config, MCP servers, skills, memory, persona
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentmove
[\fB--home\fR \fIdir\fR]
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agentmove
migrates AI agent setups between OpenClaw, Hermes Agent, Claude Code, Codex
CLI, Cursor, and Gemini CLI \(em in any direction, through a portable bundle
format. Imports are dry-run by default, existing files are backed up before
writing, likely secrets are redacted on export, and every lossy mapping is
reported as a warning.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B export \fIclient\fR [\fB-o\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fB--include-secrets\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Export a client's setup into a portable bundle directory (default
\fI./agentmove-bundle\fR).
.TP
.B import \fIclient\fR [\fB-i\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fB--apply\fR] [\fB--replace-mcp\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Import a bundle into a client. Dry-run by default; \fB--apply\fR writes files
after backing up existing ones to \fI~/.agentmove/backups/<timestamp>/\fR.
Imported MCP servers are merged into the target's existing list;
\fB--replace-mcp\fR replaces it entirely.
.TP
.B convert \fIfrom\fR \fIto\fR [\fB--apply\fR] [\fB--include-secrets\fR] [\fB--replace-mcp\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Export + import in one step, without leaving a bundle on disk.
.TP
.B diff \fIfrom\fR \fIto\fR [\fB--json\fR]
Layer-by-layer structural comparison between two clients, or between a bundle
directory and a client.
.TP
.B doctor [\fB--json\fR]
Detect installed clients and inventory what agentmove can migrate from each.
.TP
.B clients [\fB--json\fR]
List supported clients and their default config locations.
.TP
.B completion \fIbash\fR|\fIzsh\fR|\fIfish\fR
Print a shell completion script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --home \fIdir\fR
Override the home directory (useful for testing and staging).
.TP
.B --json
Machine-readable JSON output (plans, warnings, per-layer summary).
.TP
.B --only \fIlayers\fR
Comma-separated subset of layers to migrate:
\fImcp\fR, \fIskills\fR, \fImemory\fR, \fIinstructions\fR, \fIpersona\fR
(on \fBexport\fR, \fBimport\fR, and \fBconvert\fR).
.TP
.B --project \fIdir\fR
Operate on the client's project-scoped files inside \fIdir\fR instead of the
home directory: \fB.mcp.json\fR/\fBCLAUDE.md\fR (claude-code),
\fBAGENTS.md\fR (codex), \fB.gemini/settings.json\fR/\fBGEMINI.md\fR (gemini),
\fB.cursor/mcp.json\fR/\fB.cursor/rules\fR (cursor). Backups go to
\fIdir\fR/.agentmove/backups. openclaw/hermes have no project scope.
.TP
.B --debug
Print a full stack trace on unexpected errors (also enabled by the
\fBAGENTMOVE_DEBUG=1\fR environment variable).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Unexpected error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (e.g. unknown client).
.TP
.B 3
Bad input data (missing or corrupt bundle or config; the message includes the
offending file path).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.agentmove/backups/
Automatic backups taken before \fB--apply\fR writes.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation at
.UR https://agentmove.zalize.com
.UE .
